# Demo 2 - "decisions survive the session". Read-only, against taska's OWN store.
# Every task on screen is real, and the notes were written by the agent that did
# the work - this is the article's claim, demonstrated rather than asserted.
#
#   make -C docs notes          # or `make -C docs all`
#
# The exact flags live in docs/Makefile, so this header and the build agree.
#
# WIDTH/HEIGHT. The search hit table needs 105 columns, so 110 is the floor - a
# wrapped table is unreadable in a way prose is not. The notes themselves were
# written with hard line breaks around 85 characters, so they do not wrap, and
# the record is 15 lines: the whole demo is 33 rows, so 34 fits it without scrolling.
#
# The subject is chosen for that shape as much as its content. A task whose notes
# are one long paragraph renders to 60+ rows once wrapped and scrolls away to a
# wall of implementation detail; this one reads end to end.

expect "$ "

show "\e[90m# months later: why does CI build for Windows when the tests are Linux-only?\e[0m"
key Enter
expect "$ "
wait 600ms

show "\e[90m# search inside what the agents wrote at the time\e[0m"
key Enter
expect "$ "
wait 400ms
type "ta list 'notes=~Windows' --columns id,title,status"
key Enter
expect "$ "
wait 3s

show "\e[90m# the answer is still there: cause, why nothing caught it, and the guard added\e[0m"
key Enter
expect "$ "
wait 400ms
type "ta show windows-build-failure --columns id,notes"
key Enter
expect "$ "
wait 6s
